     ``<target>`` is a filter or filter instance name and defaults to ``all``.
     Note that the target is an additional specifier for filters that
     support them, such as complex ``lavfi`` filter chains.
+
+``lavfi-complex-command <target> <command> <argument> [<refresh-audio>]``
+    Set a runtime option on a named filter instance in ``--lavfi-complex``.
+    The target must be an exact libavfilter instance name, for example
+    ``amix@audio_mix``. Unlike ``af-command``, this addresses the shared complex
+    graph and preserves the last successful value of each target/option across
+    seeks and input format changes. It does not replace the graph or seek.
+
+    Only runtime options are accepted. A value sent before input formats are
+    available is validated as an option and applied after graph configuration,
+    before any output frames. The retained values belong to the graph and are
+    discarded when it is replaced. An unknown target/option reports failure.
+
+    With ``refresh-audio=yes`` (default: no), replay decoded complex-graph
+    audio through fresh filter buffers at the end of the queued output. This
+    avoids waiting for old mixed samples in lookahead filters, without seeking
+    decoders or restarting playing audio/video. Replacement output is trimmed
+    at that boundary. While paused, the audio output buffers can be cleared.
+    Video inputs retain their latest frame; duplicate video output is skipped.
+
+    History is bounded to 12 seconds, 16 MiB per input, 64 MiB of audio overall
+    and 4096 frames per input. If timestamps/history do not cover the boundary,
+    the setter still applies normally without replay. Seek clears history.
 
 ``af-command <label> <command> <argument> [<target>]``
     Same as ``vf-command``, but for audio filters.
